{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1131113-how-would-you-do-a-chronicle-set-in-the-1950s","id":1131113,"title":"How would you do a chronicle set in the 1950s?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-18T21:06:25-07:00","id":1131113,"title":"How would you do a chronicle set in the 1950s?","content":"My birthday is monday and i am hoping to get W20. I am thinking about setting my first chronicle set in the 1950s, This campaign would have the good parts and the bad parts of the 50s through the lenses of a pack of Werewolves who had their first change. My question is how would certain tribes like the Silver Fangs and Silent Striders work in the 50s? Also, how would you make PENTEX work in this time period. Also, I am thinking about adding in a Weaver front that is basically the American version of Shinzui. So, what kind of tech in the 50s would be considered Weaver-Tech?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T08:56:14-07:00","id":1131296,"title":"","content":"Well, at the time, the use of lead in various places, such as gasoline, was still widespread, so there's that terrible issue to deal with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T11:56:56-07:00","id":1131372,"title":"","content":"The tribes themselves don't really change all that much through time just individual character concepts and how their kinfolk operate. I don't see all that much difference for Silver Fangs and Silent Striders.<br /> <br /> The tribe with the biggest change would be the Glass Walkers since they are the only ones who really change through passage of time and evolve to reflect human society. Several modern camps wouldn't exist yet and you can invent new ones that will briefly flourish for a few decades.<br /> <br /> Weaver-Tech in the current setting is usually just current near-future sci-fi concepts. So for the 1950s look to the same. Most of their near future sci-fi would be based on 1) safe nuclear power, 2) jet age stuff, 3) space age stuff, and 4) big mainframe computers. New plastics and new electronics are creating a world we take for granted now but would be mindblowing back then. Also just transplant some of the 1960s and early 1970s real world technology to the 1950s and say it works because it is Weaver tech. Think of very early James Bond movies of the 1960s, and you'll see exotic technology put to use in ways PCs often use them in game.<br /> <br /> Tech devices that seem magical in the 1950s might include:<br /> <br /> 1) Mobile telephones (think the huge blocky phones from the 1980s, but they'll only work in a limited distance since they run on only one cell tower built in the city)<br /> 2) Direct dialing with secure speech (until the 1960s, if you called someone you need to go through a switchboard operator, and the line was often party lines multiple people would use)<br /> 3) Video phone, but sorry it won't be mobile<br /> 4) The laser<br /> 5) Audio casette players/recorders<br /> 6) Kevlar body armor<br /> 7) Bar Codes and scanners that can record inventory<br /> 8) Secret planes that have supersonic flight<br /> 9) Handheld calculators, especially those which can perform the higher math functions<br /> 10) Things that boost car performance (like the fuel injector) so you have a car that can outperform all others<br /> 11) Many kinds of pharmaceutical drugs","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T18:03:19-07:00","id":1131534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1131113-how-would-you-do-a-chronicle-set-in-the-1950s?p=1131372#post1131372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The tribes themselves don't really change all that much through time just individual character concepts and how their kinfolk operate. I don't see all that much difference for Silver Fangs and Silent Striders.<br /> <br /> The tribe with the biggest change would be the Glass Walkers since they are the only ones who really change through passage of time and evolve to reflect human society. Several modern camps wouldn't exist yet and you can invent new ones that will briefly flourish for a few decades.<br /> <br /> Weaver-Tech in the current setting is usually just current near-future sci-fi concepts. So for the 1950s look to the same. Most of their near future sci-fi would be based on 1) safe nuclear power, 2) jet age stuff, 3) space age stuff, and 4) big mainframe computers. New plastics and new electronics are creating a world we take for granted now but would be mindblowing back then. Also just transplant some of the 1960s and early 1970s real world technology to the 1950s and say it works because it is Weaver tech. Think of very early James Bond movies of the 1960s, and you'll see exotic technology put to use in ways PCs often use them in game.<br /> <br /> Tech devices that seem magical in the 1950s might include:<br /> <br /> 1) Mobile telephones (think the huge blocky phones from the 1980s, but they'll only work in a limited distance since they run on only one cell tower built in the city)<br /> 2) Direct dialing with secure speech (until the 1960s, if you called someone you need to go through a switchboard operator, and the line was often party lines multiple people would use)<br /> 3) Video phone, but sorry it won't be mobile<br /> 4) The laser<br /> 5) Audio casette players/recorders<br /> 6) Kevlar body armor<br /> 7) Bar Codes and scanners that can record inventory<br /> 8) Secret planes that have supersonic flight<br /> 9) Handheld calculators, especially those which can perform the higher math functions<br /> 10) Things that boost car performance (like the fuel injector) so you have a car that can outperform all others<br /> 11) Many kinds of pharmaceutical drugs</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite. WeaverTech will have a spirit in it or its composition, and operate as a fetish, and be purchased with the Fetish background, in the manner of technofetishes. Merely cutting edge stuff instead has a Device rating. For a modern example, highly advanced prostheses can be had relatively easily for humans as a Device, but for Garou and Fera, they have to be WeaverTech fetishes in order to be both physically and spiritually compatible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T19:44:34-07:00","id":1131576,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the advice so far. I wonder how PENTEX would work in a 50s chronicle? Also, I am thinking about including the greaser subculture that appeared during that time. How could I give that subculture a Werewolf twist?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T01:23:25-07:00","id":1131651,"title":"","content":"Environmental issues are mostly unknown by the masses in the '50, so there would be a lot of room for Pentex' Wyrm-tainted industries. Drilling the oil in the middle west and US oceans, the growing car industry, uranium mines in Canada, bribing public officers to get building permits on wild zones or natural parks, building weapons for the government or making napalm for the Vietnam war... they could even skim on the after-war reconstruction efforts in Europe or the humanitarian aids, Mafia style. Or they could have money in the music industry! It's a bit too early for death metal, sadly.<br /> The best way is to look at history books (or Wikipedia pages) for noteworthy events and wonder: &quot;how would a Pentex CEO exploit that; or maybe they caused it, even?&quot;.<br /> Just remember: the Pentex is powerful because has tentacles everywhere, but they are not in charge of any nation. They can't do everything they want, they need to worm (heh) their way in.<br /> <br /> I'd also say to be careful with Weaver-tech: the sci-fi theme would be probably well fitting for a Mage campaign, but not so much expected in a Werewolf one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13673,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","user":"Maris Streck","date":". 08-21-2017, 05:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T12:13:51-07:00","id":1131827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1131113-how-would-you-do-a-chronicle-set-in-the-1950s?p=1131534#post1131534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WeaverTech will have a spirit in it or its composition, and operate as a fetish, and be purchased with the Fetish background, in the manner of technofetishes. Merely cutting edge stuff instead has a Device rating.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know the difference between a Fetish and a Device. I was giving the OP examples for inspiration for whatever he wanted to do.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T13:06:32-07:00","id":1131853,"title":"","content":"The Glass Walkers are in flux in the 50's changing between the Maifa based group to the wall street wolves. The 50's will mark the height of the power of the real world Mafia..<br /> <br /> \u200b&quot;Greaser sub-culture&quot; screams Bone Gnawers at least to my mind. look at the &quot;General Lee&quot; totem and switch to a drag race theme. <br /> <br /> \u200bPossible complications: <br /> \u200bF.B.I notice investigation this is the height of both the red and lavender scares.<br /> \u200bAmerica begins the change from family farms to Industrial farms.<br /> \u200bBeat poets/Hippie culture this is the beginning of the movement.<br /> \u200bPentex will mostly be concerned with Premium Oil and will have fewer subsidiaries.<br /> \u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}